    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "222c48a3_0c204be8",
        "filename": "board/phaser/gpio.inc",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 78,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003000
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-07-10T18:00:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e \u003e \u003e So we are intentionally waking on rising edge?\n\u003e \u003e \n\u003e \u003e We can select only one of the two i.e. rising or falling edge: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/master/chip/npcx/system-npcx7.c#70\n\u003e \n\u003e OK. By why rising? Just so we don\u0027t double reset? VCC1_RST# being driven low and waking all at the same time?\n\nYes. My idea is that the EC comes out of hibernate only when EC_RST_ODL is de-asserted.\n\nIdeally it should not be a problem even if we wake the EC from hibernate on falling edge because it will cause the EC to come out of hibernate and be held in reset until the signal is de-asserted. I was just worried if this could lead to any race conditions. Probably not?\n\nActually giving it some more thought, if we were in this situation:\n1. EC goes into PSL hibernate\n2. Now H1 or servo asserts EC_RST_ODL\n\nAt this point, H1 or servo expects the EC to be held in reset and not hibernate. But from EC\u0027s standpoint, all of the EC except PSL is held in reset. Even though most of EC is held in reset, it seems logically correct to wake on falling edge so that entire EC can be held in reset. Thoughts?\n\n\n\u003e \n\u003e \u003e \n\u003e \u003e \u003e And why is MECH_PWR_BTN not marked with HIB_WAKE_LOW?\n\u003e \u003e \n\u003e \u003e By default, the assumption is that a pin is HIB_WAKE_LOW if GPIO_HIB_WAKE_HIGH is not set.\n\u003e \n\u003e I see. That\u0027s not very descriptive when looking at this gpio.inc. We should probably mark it up as such.\n\nI will add some comments.\n\n\u003e \n\u003e \u003e \n\u003e \u003e \u003e  Are we only waking on rising edge of that?\n\u003e \u003e \n\u003e \u003e We wake on falling edge. Way to verify this:\n\u003e \u003e On EC console: hibernate\n\u003e \u003e In chroot: dut-control pwr_button:press\n\u003e \u003e \n\u003e \u003e This wakes the EC up from PSL hibernate.",
      "parentUuid": "9e20d5f1_7c520eaf",
      "revId": "66d217cbf409de9c8fce13bd0b04efd2959f4569",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "186d6c24_02dd9f81",
        "filename": "board/phaser/gpio.inc",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 78,
